# #675: size budgets in scripts/agent_budgets.py and scripts/skill_phases.py
# measure raw checked-out bytes. Without a pin, a file's byte count -- and
# therefore whether it is "under budget" -- is a property of the checkout
# (LF on POSIX, CRLF on a fresh Windows clone), not of the file. This makes
# every checkout agree: text files normalize to LF on checkout everywhere,
# so `len(path.read_bytes())` means the same thing on every platform.
*		text=auto eol=lf
*.png		binary
